    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "x-api-key",
              "value": "YOUR_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"
            },
            {
              "name": "anthropic-version",
              "value": "2023-06-01"
            },
            {
              "name": "content-type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ model: \"claude-sonnet-5\", max_tokens: 1024, messages: [ { role: \"user\", content: \"You are doing quality control on a video clip generated by an AI clipping tool, before it goes back to a client.\n\nCLIENT BRIEF:\n\" + $('Normalize Job Input').item.json.brief + \"\n\nCLIP UNDER REVIEW:\nTitle: \" + ($json.title || \"(no title)\") + \"\nDuration: \" + ($json.duration || \"unknown\") + \"s\nURL: \" + ($json.url || $json.download_url || \"\") + \"\nTranscript: \" + ($json.transcript || \"(not provided)\") + \"\n\nCheck the clip against the brief on these points:\n1. Does it match what the brief asked for (topic, tone, length limit)?\n2. Does it stand alone without extra context (a viewer who wasn't on the call understands it)?\n3. Is the title strong and accurate?\n4. Is there any risky cut — a sentence cut mid-thought, a promise or claim taken out of context, anything that could embarrass the client?\n\nThis is a starter rubric, not the client's real standardised workflow rules — replace this prompt once those are written down.\n\nReply with ONLY valid JSON, no other text, in this exact shape:\n{\\\"verdict\\\": \\\"pass\\\" or \\\"review\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"one or two sentence explanation\\\"}\" } ] }) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "36bdd390-44d0-4357-8077-b000f6970ed4",
      "name": "Claude: QC Review",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        1680,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "const items = $input.all();\nconst splitItems = $('Split Clips').all();\nconst brief = $('Normalize Job Input').item.json.brief;\nconst clientName = $('Normalize Job Input').item.json.client_name;\nconst toEmail = $('Normalize Job Input').item.json.notify_email || 'YOUR_TEAM@yourdomain.com';\n\nconst passed = [];\nconst review = [];\n\nitems.forEach((item, i) => {\n  const clip = (splitItems[i] && splitItems[i].json) || {};\n  let verdict = { verdict: 'review', reason: 'Could not parse the QC response - check manually.' };\n  try {\n    const text = item.json.content[0].text;\n    const parsed = JSON.parse(text);\n    if (parsed && parsed.verdict) verdict = parsed;\n  } catch (e) {\n    // leave default \"review\" verdict above\n  }\n\n  const row = {\n    title: clip.title || 'Untitled clip',\n    url: clip.url || clip.download_url || '',\n    reason: verdict.reason || ''\n  };\n\n  (verdict.verdict === 'pass' ? passed : review).push(row);\n});\n\nfunction renderRows(rows) {\n  if (!rows.length) return '<p style=\"color:#888;margin:0 0 16px;\">None</p>';\n  return '<ul style=\"margin:0 0 16px;padding-left:20px;\">' + rows.map(r =>\n    '<li style=\"margin-bottom:8px;\"><strong>' + r.title + '</strong>' +\n    (r.url ? ' &mdash; <a href=\"' + r.url + '\">' + r.url + '</a>' : '') +\n    (r.reason ? '<br><span style=\"color:#555;\">' + r.reason + '</span>' : '') +\n    '</li>'\n  ).join('') + '</ul>';\n}\n\nconst html =\n  '<h2>Rushes QC summary &mdash; ' + (clientName || 'Untitled job') + '</h2>' +\n  '<p><strong>Brief:</strong> ' + (brief || '') + '</p>' +\n  '<h3>&#9989; Passed (' + passed.length + ')</h3>' + renderRows(passed) +\n  '<h3>&#9888;&#65039; Needs a look (' + review.length + ')</h3>' + renderRows(review);\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    to_email: toEmail,\n    subject: 'Rushes QC: ' + (clientName || 'job') + ' — ' + passed.length + ' passed, ' + review.length + ' to review',\n    html\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "id": "70d48f63-ff6b-4ed6-9cde-c6fa101e70e0",
      "name": "Build QC Summary",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1920,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.resend.com/emails",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
